<attribute name="refinedDescription" nodeId="a59c2eca">&lt;p&gt;
    Define the process by performing the following:
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Gather and review the requirements for batch automation, such as what jobs or processes will need to be automated
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Create a list of the exact jobs requiring automation along with a brief description of the job, grouped by process
        and functional area
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Work with both functional and technical stakeholders to determine the time and frequency for each job. The
        information for each job should include, but is not limited to: 
        &lt;ul&gt;
            &lt;li&gt;
                what time and day(s) should the job be executed
            &lt;/li&gt;
            &lt;li&gt;
                how often should the job be executed
            &lt;/li&gt;
            &lt;li&gt;
                dependent jobs or processes
            &lt;/li&gt;
            &lt;li&gt;
                error handling (e.g., what happens if the job fails)
            &lt;/li&gt;
            &lt;li&gt;
                requesting or owning group
            &lt;/li&gt;
        &lt;/ul&gt;
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Create the consolidated batch scheduling document, building in the times and dependencies
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Share the consolidated document with the stakeholders for final confirmation. This can be an iterative process if
        corrections are required.&lt;br /&gt;
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;</attribute>
</Element>
